WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }
::cue(c.colora8c7fa) { color: #a8c7fa; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Premium</c></b>
Keep the project alive: <c.colora8c7fa>ko-fi.com/not6ip</c>

2
00:00:19.580 --> 00:00:24.950
I grabbed hold, digging in my claws
te ni totte tsume o tateta

3
00:00:24.950 --> 00:00:28.380
but the future
sono mirai wa

4
00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:34.600
blurred together, colors running
nijimu iro ni kasunde mieta

5
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:41.200
A red that can swallow even summer's hues
natsu no iro mo nuritsubusu you na aka ni

6
00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:47.920
bokura no koe kakikesareteiku you de
now attempts to blot out our voices

7
00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:54.660
Move those halting feet of yours
tachidomaru sono ashi o fumidasou ze

8
00:00:54.660 --> 00:01:01.300
Don't let stand the lies for show
misekake no uso yarisugosu yori

9
00:01:01.300 --> 00:01:07.550
I'll give up countless mornings for my vows
nandome no asa chikai to hikikaeru yo

10
00:01:07.550 --> 00:01:16.100
For the dream that we shared
bokura ga miteita yume

11
00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:35.870
<b>The Height of Folly</b>

12
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.550
All ships, prepare for bombardment!

13
00:01:43.060 --> 00:01:45.400
Retreat! Retreat!

14
00:01:46.860 --> 00:01:49.940
All soldiers, evacuate the island!
Board your ships!

15
00:01:49.920 --> 00:01:53.010
"JUSTICE"

16
00:01:50.650 --> 00:01:53.010
What happened at the center of the island?!

17
00:01:53.490 --> 00:01:56.200
I don't know! We'll just follow the order!

18
00:02:04.920 --> 00:02:07.500
St. Saturn! Admiral Borsalino!

19
00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:11.130
It's dangerous.
Please proceed to your ship promptly!

20
00:02:11.510 --> 00:02:14.300
Kizaru and I will stay here.

21
00:02:14.300 --> 00:02:16.220
As soon as preparations are complete,

22
00:02:17.390 --> 00:02:19.680
commence bombardment!

23
00:02:20.180 --> 00:02:21.980
What?! But...

24
00:02:25.020 --> 00:02:26.310
Go.

25
00:02:28.060 --> 00:02:29.020
Yes, sir!

26
00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:34.030
Won't this...

27
00:02:34.030 --> 00:02:37.700
Won't this all be over
if you just kill me?!

28
00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:38.990
St. Saturn!

29
00:02:40.910 --> 00:02:42.750
Egghead...

30
00:02:42.750 --> 00:02:47.670
...houses the latest research findings
from every field of study!

31
00:02:47.670 --> 00:02:51.960
If you destroy it, scientific progress
will be set back by 100 years!

32
00:02:51.960 --> 00:02:54.550
Revoke the Buster Call!

33
00:02:55.720 --> 00:02:57.430
Please, Kizaru!

34
00:03:01.930 --> 00:03:04.520
Is there something more
you are hiding from us?

35
00:03:06.310 --> 00:03:07.940
That is probably...

36
00:03:09.270 --> 00:03:12.320
...also troublesome
for the World Government.

37
00:03:13.530 --> 00:03:15.780
We do not need progress!

38
00:03:18.740 --> 00:03:20.240
I'm begging you!

39
00:03:21.740 --> 00:03:24.000
For the sake of humanity!

40
00:03:28.040 --> 00:03:29.420
Oh...

41
00:03:30.290 --> 00:03:32.500
I forgot to tell you...

42
00:03:35.090 --> 00:03:38.300
It is about the ship
that escaped the island yesterday.

43
00:03:38.930 --> 00:03:41.760
I have already issued an order
to pursue and strike it.

44
00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:48.850
Because there might be someone aboard
who learned something about the Void Century.

45
00:03:53.690 --> 00:03:56.320
To make sure none of them survive...

46
00:03:58.030 --> 00:03:59.990
I sent a warship.

47
00:04:08.960 --> 00:04:10.960
How could you do that?!

48
00:04:10.960 --> 00:04:12.710
They don't know anything!

49
00:04:12.710 --> 00:04:14.750
They're innocent people!

50
00:04:14.750 --> 00:04:18.930
You got them involved, Vegapunk!

51
00:04:20.970 --> 00:04:23.850
Just like the people of Ohara,
you broke the law...

52
00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.060
...succumbed to the urge for discovery

53
00:04:33.360 --> 00:04:35.610
and delved into the past.

54
00:04:46.870 --> 00:04:48.790
Pacifistas, remain on the island!

55
00:04:48.790 --> 00:04:50.580
Other soldiers, get to your ships!

56
00:04:51.210 --> 00:04:54.540
As soon as preparations are complete,
we’ll commence bombardment!

57
00:04:54.540 --> 00:04:57.170
Ship 54, prepared!

58
00:04:57.170 --> 00:04:59.510
Ship 21, prepared!

59
00:04:59.920 --> 00:05:01.430
We're ready to fire!

60
00:05:08.220 --> 00:05:11.060
Hurry! Get in the Vacuum Rocket!

61
00:05:11.060 --> 00:05:14.060
While Vegapunk is distracting them!

62
00:05:14.440 --> 00:05:16.980
The meeting point
is the rear entrance of the Labophase!

63
00:05:18.360 --> 00:05:21.490
We'll leave Egghead
once everyone has arrived!

64
00:05:21.490 --> 00:05:22.610
Okay!

65
00:05:23.240 --> 00:05:25.700
Sanji! What about Vegapunk?!

66
00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:29.330
Don't worry, Bonney-chan!

67
00:05:29.330 --> 00:05:31.040
I'll get him!

68
00:05:31.910 --> 00:05:34.080
We’ll leave it to you, Sanji!

69
00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.920
Count on me!

70
00:05:41.010 --> 00:05:44.010
Nami-san, it's me! What's your status?

71
00:05:44.260 --> 00:05:46.180
We're already at the rear entrance!

72
00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:48.260
What's all the noise down there?!

73
00:05:48.240 --> 00:05:54.650
Labophase

74
00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:50.180
Well...

75
00:05:50.680 --> 00:05:54.650
Back








entrance

76
00:05:53.890 --> 00:05:54.690
What?!

77
00:05:54.980 --> 00:05:56.520
The Buster Call?!

78
00:05:58.270 --> 00:06:00.900
This island is finished!

79
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:07.410
How many times are we gonna have to
deal with a Buster Call?!

80
00:06:09.700 --> 00:06:12.120
I'm worried about Stella...

81
00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:13.080
Swiftly!

82
00:06:13.080 --> 00:06:15.920
We gotta run! Hurry up, everyone!

83
00:06:18.090 --> 00:06:19.170
Robin!

84
00:06:20.300 --> 00:06:23.380
Everything's fine,
so you can keep resting.

85
00:06:24.510 --> 00:06:26.840
Sanji-kun? What is Luffy doing?

86
00:06:26.840 --> 00:06:28.350
He's there, right?

87
00:06:28.350 --> 00:06:30.930
Franky and Bonney went down there, too!

88
00:06:31.430 --> 00:06:33.810
He's not in my sight, but he's fine!

89
00:06:33.810 --> 00:06:35.440
Tell me the status on your end!

90
00:06:36.270 --> 00:06:39.730
Zoro is still being held up by Lucci...

91
00:06:40.150 --> 00:06:42.610
Jinbe is heading there
to put a stop to that.

92
00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:45.490
If we leave Zoro, he'll get lost.

93
00:06:46.070 --> 00:06:47.160
And...

94
00:06:47.570 --> 00:06:50.950
...Brook went to help Lilith,
who remained at the Sunny.

95
00:06:51.330 --> 00:06:53.500
But there is a problem.

96
00:06:54.040 --> 00:06:58.830
The escape plan to have the Vegaforce-01
carry us from here is no longer viable.

97
00:06:59.590 --> 00:07:02.420
Because it was destroyed by Kizaru!

98
00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:05.800
What?! Then how do we escape from here?!

99
00:07:05.800 --> 00:07:06.880
Well...

100
00:07:07.220 --> 00:07:10.260
Looks like Brook has an idea...

101
00:07:13.430 --> 00:07:16.770
Well, to me,

102
00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:22.110
moving a ship over land is a piece of cake!

103
00:07:24.070 --> 00:07:26.700
This is amazing, Bone!

104
00:07:27.450 --> 00:07:30.830
With this,
we'll reach the rear entrance in no time!

105
00:07:33.290 --> 00:07:38.000
Freezing Island Clouds and letting the ship
slide on them was a great idea!

106
00:07:39.880 --> 00:07:44.210
It's an honor to be praised
by the world's greatest genius!

107
00:07:45.130 --> 00:07:47.420
This is fun!

108
00:07:47.420 --> 00:07:50.010
And how are we going to stop?

109
00:07:50.930 --> 00:07:53.760
Oh, I haven't thought about that.

110
00:07:57.350 --> 00:07:59.600
We're going to fall then!

111
00:07:59.900 --> 00:08:02.190
What are you going to do?!

112
00:08:02.190 --> 00:08:06.150
What should I do, Lilith-san?!

113
00:08:07.570 --> 00:08:09.450
Think of something already!

114
00:08:22.380 --> 00:08:25.710
The barrier is still up at the Labophase.

115
00:08:25.710 --> 00:08:27.210
All ships!

116
00:08:27.210 --> 00:08:30.090
The target is Egghead's urban area.

117
00:08:30.090 --> 00:08:34.140
Destroy the central factory
and the future city!

118
00:08:38.640 --> 00:08:41.060
Start firing!

119
00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:53.660
Wait! We haven't boarded yet!

120
00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:02.330
W-Watch out for the Pacifistas!

121
00:09:30.900 --> 00:09:33.780
Egghead...

122
00:09:49.170 --> 00:09:53.380
Departing Fabiriophase, bound for Labophase.
We are now departing.

123
00:09:54.260 --> 00:09:55.510
All right!

124
00:09:55.970 --> 00:09:58.510
Let's go, Vacuum Rocket!

125
00:09:58.970 --> 00:10:00.350
Launch!

126
00:10:05.850 --> 00:10:08.770
What the hell is this?! So fast!

127
00:10:09.690 --> 00:10:12.440
The transit duration is 32 seconds.

128
00:10:25.960 --> 00:10:27.920
Sacred Murakumo Sword.

129
00:10:40.890 --> 00:10:42.600
Damn Kizaru!

130
00:10:43.270 --> 00:10:46.100
Bonney-chan! I'm coming!

131
00:10:51.440 --> 00:10:52.610
Pacifistas.

132
00:10:53.990 --> 00:10:55.820
Shoot Bonney and Kuma...

133
00:11:00.910 --> 00:11:02.490
...dead!

134
00:11:04.540 --> 00:11:06.710
It is just exquisite!

135
00:11:09.960 --> 00:11:13.460
The daughter he sacrificed himself to save...

136
00:11:15.300 --> 00:11:19.050
...is now being slain by his own clone.
What utter foolishness.

137
00:11:24.180 --> 00:11:26.390
A fitting end for the insect she is...

138
00:11:30.810 --> 00:11:33.230
It is the height of folly!

139
00:11:42.160 --> 00:11:43.410
Dad!

140
00:11:50.210 --> 00:11:51.340
Bonney...

141
00:11:52.000 --> 00:11:55.550
When I heard you became a pirate,

142
00:11:55.550 --> 00:11:59.890
the worst possible scenario
flashed through my mind.

143
00:12:01.010 --> 00:12:05.640
It is, by the Navy's command,
the Pacifistas in your father's likeness...

144
00:12:06.140 --> 00:12:08.060
...shooting you...

145
00:12:09.600 --> 00:12:11.860
...without recognizing you
as their daughter!

146
00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.650
Bonney-chan!

147
00:12:20.570 --> 00:12:22.620
I can't eat anymore...

148
00:12:22.620 --> 00:12:24.790
Hey! He's Straw Hat, isn't he?!

149
00:12:25.200 --> 00:12:28.620
Oh no...
I can't move, I'm too full...

150
00:12:28.620 --> 00:12:31.630
Capture him now! He's an Emperor of the Sea!

151
00:12:40.630 --> 00:12:43.350
Escape vessel destruction failed...

152
00:12:43.350 --> 00:12:46.560
C-Contact Kizaru-san...

153
00:12:58.360 --> 00:13:02.030
...and tell him they are heading for Egghead!

154
00:13:08.790 --> 00:13:10.750
Look at them goin’ at it!

155
00:13:10.750 --> 00:13:13.210
Just like the paper said!

156
00:13:19.630 --> 00:13:22.090
He digested all that food?!

157
00:13:22.090 --> 00:13:24.090
He might devour me if I get closer...

158
00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:26.100
So he's not human after all?

159
00:13:29.600 --> 00:13:30.640
That was close!

160
00:13:34.770 --> 00:13:37.360
Oh no! We're about to be
engulfed in flames!

161
00:13:37.360 --> 00:13:39.860
We can't stay on this island any longer!

162
00:13:46.030 --> 00:13:48.290
Though he is an Emperor,
we'll all do it together!

163
00:13:48.290 --> 00:13:50.830
On the count of three,
we'll put Sea Prism Stone cuffs on him!

164
00:13:52.620 --> 00:13:53.960
One, two, three!

165
00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:57.250
Board your ship!

166
00:13:57.250 --> 00:13:59.000
Move! Move!

167
00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.590
Egghead is done for!

168
00:14:02.630 --> 00:14:05.840
Burn everything down
starting from the shore! Shoot!

169
00:14:12.180 --> 00:14:14.230
Kuma! Bonney!

170
00:14:15.690 --> 00:14:18.610
Hey! Can you hear me, Atlas?!

171
00:14:21.860 --> 00:14:24.910
Shoot that foolish family,
once and for all!

172
00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:29.740
Atlas! Tell Bonney!

173
00:14:31.750 --> 00:14:33.370
Bonney-chan!

174
00:14:36.580 --> 00:14:38.290
I got it, Stella!

175
00:14:40.340 --> 00:14:41.210
Bonney!

176
00:14:42.260 --> 00:14:43.420
Atlas!

177
00:14:52.100 --> 00:14:53.980
Don't shoot!

178
00:14:53.980 --> 00:14:56.390
Dad!

179
00:14:56.680 --> 00:14:58.860
Help us escape...

180
00:14:58.860 --> 00:15:00.860
...from this island!

181
00:15:05.780 --> 00:15:07.450
Hm? What's wrong?!

182
00:15:07.450 --> 00:15:08.910
I think I heard a voice...

183
00:15:08.910 --> 00:15:09.780
What?!

184
00:15:10.240 --> 00:15:13.120
How can you hear anything
in this deafening noise?

185
00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:17.000
What?

186
00:15:22.420 --> 00:15:25.130
H-Hey, look at the Pacifistas!

187
00:15:25.510 --> 00:15:26.970
Why are they turning this way?!

188
00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:39.100
The Pacifistas have gone rogue!

189
00:15:50.740 --> 00:15:53.740
I had only one concern.

190
00:15:57.660 --> 00:15:58.830
Bonney.

191
00:15:59.710 --> 00:16:00.830
I was worried...

192
00:16:02.250 --> 00:16:05.210
...that you might be killed
by your own beloved father.

193
00:16:12.300 --> 00:16:13.260
Kuma.

194
00:16:14.010 --> 00:16:15.220
I was worried...

195
00:16:15.850 --> 00:16:18.850
...that you would harm your beloved daughter
with your own hands.

196
00:16:20.900 --> 00:16:24.400
That is a tragedy I couldn't allow to happen!

197
00:16:26.400 --> 00:16:27.990
That is why I...

198
00:16:28.860 --> 00:16:33.240
...programmed something
into all the Kuma lookalike units.

199
00:16:35.330 --> 00:16:36.080
So...

200
00:16:36.580 --> 00:16:41.540
...even if he is given commands
by the world's highest authority,

201
00:16:43.250 --> 00:16:46.750
even if he turns the whole world against him,

202
00:16:49.380 --> 00:16:50.510
Bonney,

203
00:16:51.430 --> 00:16:53.390
Kuma will always...

204
00:16:53.930 --> 00:16:56.010
...be on your side!

205
00:16:58.600 --> 00:17:01.690
This is just a selfish wish of mine!

206
00:17:03.440 --> 00:17:04.650
So...

207
00:17:07.860 --> 00:17:09.900
...I know well...

208
00:17:10.820 --> 00:17:13.950
...there are unavoidable consequences...

209
00:17:16.410 --> 00:17:19.660
...for doing such a thing!

210
00:17:22.120 --> 00:17:23.330
Vegapunk!

211
00:17:27.340 --> 00:17:30.090
Dammit! Vegapunk!

212
00:17:30.550 --> 00:17:32.550
Eliminate them, Kizaru.

213
00:17:34.590 --> 00:17:35.850
Immediately!

214
00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:54.240
Kizaru!

215
00:17:54.240 --> 00:17:55.490
Damn!

216
00:17:55.490 --> 00:17:57.780
I'll cut you both in half.

217
00:17:57.780 --> 00:18:01.160
This won't hurt, Bonney.

218
00:18:24.730 --> 00:18:25.560
Straw Hat?

219
00:18:26.270 --> 00:18:27.270
Where is he?

220
00:18:30.980 --> 00:18:33.820
Full belly, full power!

221
00:18:39.200 --> 00:18:42.120
This is getting fun!

222
00:18:44.410 --> 00:18:45.830
Bonney-chan, are you okay?!

223
00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:50.090
The island is wiggling!

224
00:18:50.090 --> 00:18:51.590
We have a bigger problem!

225
00:18:52.550 --> 00:18:54.380
Stop the Pacifistas!

226
00:19:06.640 --> 00:19:08.190
Vegapunk!

227
00:19:09.440 --> 00:19:10.480
Vegapunk!

228
00:19:11.860 --> 00:19:13.940
Vegapunk! Let's run!

229
00:19:13.940 --> 00:19:15.110
You'll be killed!

230
00:19:33.340 --> 00:19:34.710
This rhythm...

231
00:19:38.430 --> 00:19:39.680
Nika?

232
00:19:39.930 --> 00:19:42.640
Yes, he is my hero.

233
00:19:42.890 --> 00:19:46.390
He will come laughing,
moving to this rhythm.

234
00:19:56.650 --> 00:19:57.820
Bonney...

235
00:19:58.530 --> 00:20:02.030
So you didn't realize it...

236
00:20:02.530 --> 00:20:07.210
I couldn't be certain either,
until I saw it for myself.

237
00:20:07.790 --> 00:20:12.790
The very Straw Hat Luffy
who Kuma had his eyes on,

238
00:20:13.500 --> 00:20:17.800
was Nika, the Sun God!

239
00:20:21.470 --> 00:20:22.720
What?

240
00:20:24.260 --> 00:20:26.350
Kuma was right...

241
00:20:27.890 --> 00:20:31.020
The Buster Call is futile.

242
00:20:34.360 --> 00:20:38.900
Because there are people all over the world
who have been waiting for him...

243
00:20:39.610 --> 00:20:41.860
...for centuries!

244
00:20:42.390 --> 00:20:45.100
Northeast
coast

Egghead

245
00:20:43.280 --> 00:20:47.080
We're off the northeast coast!
There is a humongous ship approaching us!

246
00:20:48.120 --> 00:20:49.960
That's definitely them!

247
00:20:49.960 --> 00:20:53.210
But I thought they disbanded
over 100 years ago!

248
00:20:53.210 --> 00:20:54.920
Why are they here?!

249
00:20:55.710 --> 00:20:56.960
Should we stop?!

250
00:20:57.210 --> 00:20:59.380
No, we'll charge ahead!

251
00:21:01.590 --> 00:21:04.260
They're coming this way!

252
00:21:04.470 --> 00:21:06.100
Shoot!

253
00:21:13.270 --> 00:21:16.480
Damn! Why are the Giants here?!

254
00:21:16.940 --> 00:21:20.700
They keep asking "Why," Dorry!

255
00:21:20.700 --> 00:21:24.910
Don't they know that everything in this world
happens for a reason, Brogy?!

256
00:21:31.790 --> 00:21:34.880
We're here for you, Straw Hat!

257
00:21:37.590 --> 00:21:40.090
Sun God!

258
00:21:40.300 --> 00:21:42.050
Emergency!

259
00:21:42.050 --> 00:21:44.890
The Giant Pirate Crew has appeared!

260
00:21:53.880 --> 00:21:58.100
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop, beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipapii papipo, piipapii

261
00:21:58.100 --> 00:22:02.320
Beep-bup-beep, bup-bip-bop beep-beep-beep-bup-bop
Piipapii papipo, piipapii papipo piipii pipopii, pipopiipii

